on/math-academy-id "q-37900" :question/problem "If $f(x)$ is continuous at $x=-1$ and $f(-1)=-3,$ then what is ${lim}_{x\\to {(-1)}^{-}}f(x)?$" :question/worked-solution "We're told that $f(x)$ is continuous at $x=-1.$ According to the definition of continuity, this means that ${lim}_{x\\to (-1)}f(x)$ exists and\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to (-1)}f(x)=f(-1)=-3.\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to {(-1)}^{-}}f(x)={lim}_{x\\to (-1)}f(x)=-3.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-37900/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "70029065-69c3-585d-a6a1-cc9d2485a60a"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-37900"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-48106/selection/0cac882e457c016c9f314d89919ca330b220195498ef1b880515bf5adc44351b" :answer/id #uuid "6f19a510-9dda-5f8a-8662-fd8d75f1f3cb" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$f(x)$ is a piecewise function" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-48106/selection/918a4655fc9d82aead4c90211f8357260f208e45ecd073fa09abe2177f8718ac" :answer/id #uuid "83955748-13e1-574c-9374-a277ae228439" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$f(1)$ does not exist" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-48106/selection/5eea363a8c9cfbfcd4025ba4e1ffad0890267f3fc36b7d9363a3eb470f72afda" :answer/id #uuid "636dc83b-2078-556f-bda2-0c06efe05c9f" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "${lim}_{x\\to {1}^{+}}f(x)$ does not exist" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-48106/selection/5e3aed099302bb679fbd1ff1a455c1f9712d003f883a3008bb053e2941f18bfd" :answer/id #uuid "a8313eb5-4a7a-56c9-a3b6-7b948beef0ef" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{lim}_{x\\to {1}^{-}}f(x)\\ne {lim}_{x\\to {1}^{+}}f(x)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-48106/selection/a3464effa2c5a5bb17c35a9435f1b2f82aa5ba21a4fd6fb64d3825e9580432e6" :answer/id #uuid "a3b2c3f4-78d9-5140-a3da-258fd8f2ccb2" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "${lim}_{x\\to {1}^{-}}f(x)$ does not exist" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-48106/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "6eec9ca3-e37d-561b-aafd-39b1cb8e7283" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-48106/selection/5e3aed099302bb679fbd1ff1a455c1f9712d003f883a3008bb053e2941f18bfd" :answer-field/choices ["q-48106/selection/0cac882e457c016c9f314d89919ca330b220195498ef1b880515bf5adc44351b" "q-48106/selection/918a4655fc9d82aead4c90211f8357260f208e45ecd073fa09abe2177f8718ac" "q-48106/selection/5eea363a8c9cfbfcd4025ba4e1ffad0890267f3fc36b7d9363a3eb470f72afda" "q-48106/selection/5e3aed099302bb679fbd1ff1a455c1f9712d003f883a3008bb053e2941f18bfd" "q-48106/selection/a3464effa2c5a5bb17c35a9435f1b2f82aa5ba21a4fd6fb64d3825e9580432e6"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-48106" :question/id #uuid "5a80d358-5059-5e32-b5f6-cc17b63eac94" :question/math-academy-id "q-48106" :question/problem "For what reason does the function $f(x)$ given below have a discontinuity at $x=1?$\n\n$$\nf(x)={\\begin{aligned}x, & x\\le 1 \\\\ -x, & x>1\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Let's check the conditions necessary for $f(x)$ to be continuous at $x=1.$\n\n- $f(1)=1,$ so $f(1)$ exists. $✓$\n\n- We calculate the one-sided limits and check if they coincide:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to {1}^{-}}f(x) & ={lim}_{x\\to {1}^{-}}(x) \\\\  & =1, \\\\ {lim}_{x\\to {1}^{+}}f(x) & ={lim}_{x\\to {1}^{+}}(-x) \\\\  & =-(1) \\\\  & =-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the one-sided limits exist but are not equal. $\\,\\,\\times $ $\\,\\,\\,$\n\nTherefore, the function $f(x)$ has a discontinuity at $x=1$ because ${lim}_{x\\to {1}^{-}}f(x)\\ne {lim}_{x\\to {1}^{+}}f(x).$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-48106/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "fa1ddb40-3494-541c-b23e-b15dd98bf669"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-48106"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-104148/selection/80afab0e608479921a1376fd021450044da43017ebb6961a2a5a0bd1a8b4bb54" :answer/id #uuid "9b2c5b8c-a2b4-5ec1-aa3c-ca0fbb8e00d0" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "${lim}_{x\\to (-\\sqrt{3})}f(x)$ does not exist" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-104148/selection/10c0748e33f3401dd797e9631806f61465229670fc828af03d6fec587bd18627" :answer/id #uuid "c08c4809-ddd8-5211-acb1-2f626299cd14" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{lim}_{x\\to (-\\sqrt{3})}f(x)\\ne f(-\\sqrt{3})" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-104148/selection/30123a3cac577f3416ed194948b944f43fdc4eb36f3295215de5acf47d89cf4e" :answer/id #uuid "6ffef04f-42d1-56b8-9198-1dea1a53ed3e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{lim}_{x\\to (-\\sqrt{3})^{-}}f(x)\\ne {lim}_{x\\to (-\\sqrt{3})^{+}}f(x)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-104148/selection/0cac882e457c016c9f314d89919ca330b220195498ef1b880515bf5adc44351b" :answer/id #uuid "8fa65a2c-7495-580a-9acc-6e12591e327b" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$f(x)$ is a piecewise function" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-104148/selection/29e0a3f6e54446b74df0b693ec60170dd5fdbeb396e8e6d0c2a5a57026ab69d7" :answer/id #uuid "7003be15-2da1-5dd8-bb92-a36d2643349e" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$f(-\\sqrt{3})$ does not exist" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-104148/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "6f2313a8-c044-5d0e-bf6b-5065dd5449ce" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-104148/selection/10c0748e33f3401dd797e9631806f61465229670fc828af03d6fec587bd18627" :answer-field/choices ["q-104148/selection/80afab0e608479921a1376fd021450044da43017ebb6961a2a5a0bd1a8b4bb54" "q-104148/selection/10c0748e33f3401dd797e9631806f61465229670fc828af03d6fec587bd18627" "q-104148/selection/30123a3cac577f3416ed194948b944f43fdc4eb36f3295215de5acf47d89cf4e" "q-104148/selection/0cac882e457c016c9f314d89919ca330b220195498ef1b880515bf5adc44351b" "q-104148/selection/29e0a3f6e54446b74df0b693ec60170dd5fdbeb396e8e6d0c2a5a57026ab69d7"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-104148" :question/id #uuid "d39d4010-b0be-5ef1-9cec-21d22a7b88ee" :question/math-academy-id "q-104148" :question/problem "For what reason does the function $f(x)$ below have a discontinuity at $x=-\\sqrt{3}?$ \n\n$$\nf(x)={\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{x}^{2}+3}{3}, & x<-\\sqrt{3} \\\\ 3, & x=-\\sqrt{3} \\\\ \\frac{12}{{x}^{2}+3}, & x>-\\sqrt{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Let's check the conditions necessary for $f(x)$ to be continuous at $x=-\\sqrt{3}.$\n\n- $f(-\\sqrt{3})=3,$ so $f(-\\sqrt{3})$ exists. $✓$\n\n- We calculate the one-sided limits and find that they coincide:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to (-\\sqrt{3})^{-}}f(x) & ={lim}_{x\\to (-\\sqrt{3})^{-}}(\\frac{{x}^{2}+3}{3}) \\\\  & =\\frac{(-\\sqrt{3})^{2}+3}{3} \\\\  & =2, \\\\ {lim}_{x\\to (-\\sqrt{3})^{+}}f(x) & ={lim}_{x\\to (-\\sqrt{3})^{+}}(\\frac{12}{{x}^{2}+3}) \\\\  & =\\frac{12}{(-\\sqrt{3})^{2}+3} \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the overall limit exists and ${lim}_{x\\to (-\\sqrt{3})}f(x)=2.\\,\\,✓$ $\\,\\,\\,$\n\n- The limit of the function is not equal to the function value: ${lim}_{x\\to (-\\sqrt{3})}f(x)=2,$ while $f(-\\sqrt{3})=3.$ $\\times $\n\nTherefore, the function $f(x)$ has a discontinuity at $x=-\\sqrt{3}$ because ${lim}_{x\\to (-\\sqrt{3})}f(x)\\ne f(-\\sqrt{3}).$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-104148/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "fa1ddb40-3494-541c-b23e-b15dd98bf669"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-104148"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-104153/selection/eadb4f132857861f1e64373661b9a01bc3625cc86bcffcc32659fc4899904fe0" :answer/id #uuid "feba31f9-6a3a-58d6-abf8-8fdc6ee943ac" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-104153/selection/d971375f57c56d8a55a