cording to the definition of continuity, this means that ${lim}_{x\\to 5}f(x)$ exists and\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to 5}f(x)=f(5)=2.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to 5}\\sqrt{{x}^{3}-25f(x)} & =\\sqrt{{5}^{3}-25\\cdot 2} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{75} \\\\  & =5\\sqrt{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-104153/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "70029065-69c3-585d-a6a1-cc9d2485a60a"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-104153"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-104155/selection/681a4b64a7bb464b7f554c4e26477e3547d3c60cd353fce5dda4ae108b1c4fa5" :answer/id #uuid "f7626db6-d91b-595b-97e3-8701e4013221" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-104155/selection/3a619fab2616dab0463f9c76cb72cd9f101e45e62111356a5b0b111e062a8dcf" :answer/id #uuid "0dd3ea07-cbff-5758-9170-a2341e3862bd" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{2}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-104155/selection/c087f5dc559272d193745a4428553203b94404f681d8529e6e619348c0528d10" :answer/id #uuid "2b439bc1-88d9-58df-a770-f6057ccf23eb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{3}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-104155/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" :answer/id #uuid "f9117642-6733-53f7-bf3b-9c89f62e58b0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-104155/selection/b13ac151352392d38026eed875b911708c50c896d6c09463410ac041030163ff" :answer/id #uuid "b1877fb0-9ef0-5952-ad53-72dcf11cc56f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-104155/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "084bd079-7d65-5288-a595-ab51054fe31b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-104155/selection/c087f5dc559272d193745a4428553203b94404f681d8529e6e619348c0528d10" :answer-field/choices ["q-104155/selection/681a4b64a7bb464b7f554c4e26477e3547d3c60cd353fce5dda4ae108b1c4fa5" "q-104155/selection/3a619fab2616dab0463f9c76cb72cd9f101e45e62111356a5b0b111e062a8dcf" "q-104155/selection/c087f5dc559272d193745a4428553203b94404f681d8529e6e619348c0528d10" "q-104155/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" "q-104155/selection/b13ac151352392d38026eed875b911708c50c896d6c09463410ac041030163ff"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-104155" :question/id #uuid "fd3ee4e1-bde0-55c3-ada1-52860b4310e8" :question/math-academy-id "q-104155" :question/problem "If $f(x)$ is continuous at $x=4$ and $f(4)=-6,$ then what is ${lim}_{x\\to {4}^{+}}\\frac{(f(x))^{2}}{6x}?$" :question/worked-solution "We're told that $f(x)$ is continuous at $x=4.$ According to the definition of continuity, this means that ${lim}_{x\\to 4}f(x)$ exists, and\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to {4}^{+}}f(x)={lim}_{x\\to 4}f(x)=f(4)=-6.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to {4}^{+}}\\frac{(f(x))^{2}}{6x} & =\\frac{(-6)^{2}}{6\\cdot 4}=\\frac{3}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-104155/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "70029065-69c3-585d-a6a1-cc9d2485a60a"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-104155"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]}]
